  "limitations": [
    "Timing on Mac, recover() only, no phone/full-workflow extrapolation.",
    "One timed recover call per target/config after three warmups per case/config; rotating order.",
    "Selection deliberately includes motion, small balls and frame edges. Acceptance rates are for this sample, not whole videos.",
    "Reference masks come from the existing full model; agreement does not prove correctness.",
    "No reconstructed masks entered counting, exports or the installed app.",
    "Strict thresholds were fixed before this run; no post-hoc threshold tuning."
  ],
  "nextStep": "A separate, purpose-built lightweight mask estimator evaluated against this same fixed reference set, then first-use end-to-end timing on both phones if quality passes. Keep full-model fallback; do not change counting from appearance experiments.",
  "releaseRecommendation": "Keep the heavy replacement workflow in TestFlight. Retain validated sparse decoding and exact prediction reuse. Do not broadly market the heavy first-use workflow at the current measured delay. A public release of other functionality can be considered only with an explicit product decision about this feature.",
  "visualReview": {
    "artifact": "quality-comparison.png",
    "findings": [
      "Transported masks often cover less of the ball boundary than the retained reference. First two selected IMG_1529 examples show edge reduction.",
      "At IMG_9094 8.679s the retained rf288 reference includes shoe pixels; the transported mask removes that spill. The worst disagreement metric therefore cannot be treated as proof of worse visible accuracy.",
      "The strict-pass example still has modest contour differences. No actual replacement export or temporal stability validation was performed because the exact-clip acceptance gate failed."
    ],
    "decisionBasis": "Insufficient acceptance on IMG_1529 under the predeclared validation gates; no demonstrated phone/full-workflow benefit. Not a blanket assertion that all transported masks are inaccurate."
  },
